<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Exp Med</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Experimental Medicine</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1007</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-9538</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">4607030</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2139620</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Brief Definitive Reports</subject><subj-group><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>RESTORATION OF CELL-MEDIATED IMMUNITY TO ANIMALS BLOCKED BY A HUMORAL RESPONSE</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>MacKaness</surname><given-names>George B.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Lagrange</surname><given-names>Philippe H.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="N0x1c24840N0x35a6798">From the Trudeau Institute, Inc., Saranac Lake, New York 12983</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>9</month><year>1974</year></pub-date><volume>140</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>865</fpage><lpage>870</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>18</day><month>6</month><year>1974</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1974 by The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> The T cells which mediate delayed-type hypersensitivity (DTH) to sheep red blood cells (SRBC) are blocked by a normal humoral response and cannot be made to function by further immunization. They can be rescued to some extent by treatment with immunopotentiating agents such as cyclophosphamide (CY) which suppresses the antibody response selectively, or by BCG which interferes with the action of serum blocking factors. These two agents together can restore cell-mediated immunity completely, but a further antigenic stimulus is needed to reestablish DTH in mice blocked by a long period of continuous exposure to SRBC. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>